      "text": " <think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 78 and 79, we can use the distributive property of multiplication over addition. This property allows us to break down the multiplication into simpler parts. Specifically, we can express 79 as 78 + 1. Therefore, the product of 78 and 79 can be written as:\n\\[ 78 \\times 79 = 78 \\times (78 + 1) \\]\nUsing the distributive property, we can expand this expression:\n\\[ 78 \\times (78 + 1) = 78 \\times 78 + 78 \\times 1 \\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ 78 \\times 79 = 78^2 + 78 \\]\nNext, we need to calculate \\( 78^2 \\). We can find this by using the formula for the square of a binomial:\n\\[ (a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2 \\]\nHere, \\( a = 78 \\) and \\( b = 1 \\), so:\n\\[ 78^2 = (77 + 1)^2 = 77^2 + 2 \\times 77 \\times 1 + 1^2 \\]\nWe need to calculate \\( 77^2 \\) and \\( 77 \\times 2 \\):\n\\[ 77^2 = (70 + 7)^2 = 70^2 + 2 \\times 70 \\times 7 + 7^2 = 4900 + 980 + 49 = 5929 \\]\n\\[ 77 \\times 2 = 154 \\]\nAdding these together:\n\\[ 77^2 + 2 \\times 77 \\times 1 + 1^2 = 5929 + 154 + 1 = 6084 \\]\nSo:\n\\[ 78^2 = 6084 \\]\nNow we substitute back into our expression:\n\\[ 78 \\times 79 = 78^2 + 78 = 6084 + 78 = 6162 \\]\nTherefore, the product of 78 and 79 is:\n\\[ 78 \\times 79 = 6162 \\]\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe product of 78 and 79 is 6162.\n</answer>",
