      "text": " <think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 49 and 23, we can use the standard multiplication method. This involves multiplying each digit of one number by each digit of the other number and then adding the results. Let's break it down step by step.\n...\n</think>\n<answer>\nFirst, let's write the numbers one above the other for clarity:\n```\n  49\n\u00d7 23\n```\nWe'll start by multiplying 49 by 3 (the ones digit of 23):\n```\n  49\n\u00d7  3\n-----\n 147\n```\nNow, we need to multiply 49 by 20 (the tens digit of 23, which is 2 times 10):\n```\n  49\n\u00d7 20\n-----\n 980\n```\nTo get the final product, we add the two results together:\n```\n  147\n+980\n-----\n1127\n```\nTherefore, the product of 49 and 23 is 1127.\n</answer>",
