      "text": " <think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 81 and 61, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm. This involves multiplying each digit of one number by each digit of the other number and then adding the results. Let's break it down step by step.\n...\n</think>\n<answer>\nFirst, let's write the numbers one above the other for clarity:\n```\n   81\nx  61\n-----\n```\nWe start by multiplying 81 by 1 (the units digit of 61):\n```\n   81\nx  61\n-----\n   81  (This is 81 x 1)\n```\nNext, we multiply 81 by 6 (the tens digit of 61), but we need to remember to shift the result one place to the left because we are dealing with tens:\n```\n   81\nx  61\n-----\n   81\n+ 4860  (This is 81 x 6, shifted one place to the left)\n```\nNow, we add the two results together:\n```\n   81\n+4860\n-----\n  4941\n```\nTherefore, the product of 81 and 61 is 4941.\n</answer>",
