      "text": " <think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 73 and 74, we can use the distributive property of multiplication over addition. This property allows us to break down the multiplication into simpler parts. Specifically, we can express 74 as 73 + 1. This will help us use the formula for the product of two consecutive numbers.\n\\[\n73 \\times 74 = 73 \\times (73 + 1)\n\\]\nUsing the distributive property, we can rewrite the expression:\n\\[\n73 \\times 73 + 73 \\times 1\n\\]\nSince \\(73 \\times 1 = 73\\), the expression simplifies to:\n\\[\n73 \\times 73 + 73\n\\]\nNow, we can factor out the common term 73:\n\\[\n73 \\times (73 + 1) = 73 \\times 74\n\\]\nTo find the exact value, we can use the formula for the product of two consecutive numbers, which is:\n\\[\nn(n + 1) = n^2 + n\n\\]\nHere, \\(n = 73\\). Substituting \\(n = 73\\) into the formula:\n\\[\n73 \\times 74 = 73^2 + 73\n\\]\nNext, we calculate \\(73^2\\):\n\\[\n73^2 = 73 \\times 73\n\\]\nTo find \\(73 \\times 73\\), we can use the method of squaring a binomial:\n\\[\n73^2 = (70 + 3)^2 = 70^2 + 2 \\times 70 \\times 3 + 3^2\n\\]\nCalculating each term separately:\n\\[\n70^2 = 4900\n\\]\n\\[\n2 \\times 70 \\times 3 = 420\n\\]\n\\[\n3^2 = 9\n\\]\nAdding these together:\n\\[\n73^2 = 4900 + 420 + 9 = 5329\n\\]\nNow, we add 73 to \\(73^2\\):\n\\[\n73^2 + 73 = 5329 + 73 = 5402\n\\]\nTherefore, the product of 73 and 74 is:\n\\[\n73 \\times 74 = 5402\n\\]\n\\|\n|Assistant|<answer>\nThe product of 73 and 74 is 5402.\n</answer>>",
