      "index": 0,
      "text": " <think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 57 and 53, we can use the standard multiplication method. This involves multiplying each digit of one number by each digit of the other number and then adding the results. Alternatively, we can use the difference of squares formula, which simplifies the calculation significantly. The difference of squares formula states that \\( (a+b)(a-b) = a^2 - b^2 \\). In this case, we can rewrite 57 and 53 as \\( (55+2) \\) and \\( (55-2) \\) respectively. This allows us to use the formula with \\( a = 55 \\) and \\( b = 2 \\).\n</think>\n<answer>\nUsing the difference of squares formula:\n\\[\n(57 \\times 53) = (55 + 2)(55 - 2) = 55^2 - 2^2\n\\]\nCalculating \\( 55^2 \\):\n\\[\n55^2 = 55 \\times 55 = 3025\n\\]\nCalculating \\( 2^2 \\):\n\\[\n2^2 = 4\n\\]\nSubtracting these results:\n\\[\n3025 - 4 = 3021\n\\]\nTherefore, the product of 57 and 53 is 3021.\n</answer>",
      "logprobs": null,
      "finish_reason": "stop",
